	// StreamEvents Live updates as Server-Sent Events
	//
	// One stream per browser tab. Each SSE message has `id`, `event` (the
	// event type) and `data` (the JSON `Event` below). The server sends a
	// `heartbeat` event every 15 seconds. On reconnect, send
	// `Last-Event-ID` to receive what was missed; if that is too old, the
	// server sends `resync` and the client should refetch its queries.
	//
	// Only events the caller is allowed to see are sent. When roles,
	// assignments or group mappings change, every stream ends with
	// `resync`: the client connects again, with what the caller now holds,
	// and refetches, `/me` included. A stream reads the caller's roles
	// once subscribed, so a change while it opens is in them or ends it;
	// a `Last-Event-ID` from before a change gets `resync` instead of the
	// missed events.
